Subject: [PATCH] Use little-endian serialization for list fields and pen dashes

EMF files require little-endian integers regardless of the host architecture.
Use explicit byte order for array and coordinate fields and EXTCREATEPEN dash
patterns. Add regression tests exercising simulated big-endian struct defaults,
canonical field bytes, document generation and existing EMF fixtures.

diff --git a/pyemf3/emr.py b/pyemf3/emr.py
index 158e60c..15db3d2 100644
--- a/pyemf3/emr.py
+++ b/pyemf3/emr.py
@@ -1058,7 +1058,7 @@ class EXTCREATEPEN(CREATEPALETTE):
         self.numstyleentries = len(styleentries)
         if styleentries:
             self.unhandleddata = struct.pack(
-                "i"*self.numstyleentries, *styleentries)
+                "<"+"i"*self.numstyleentries, *styleentries)
 
     def hasHandle(self):
         return True
diff --git a/pyemf3/field.py b/pyemf3/field.py
